{"component_id_namespace":"ec077a53-0b40-5f21-b1fe-a62094d2476b","component_schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","components":[{"attributes":{"code":"TMC","legacy_node_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:2.40.160","page_type":"section"},"citation":"2.40.160","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.40.160","content_hash":"24c5e0a742b55da0e0af93d48ba8513d3ae3dd68e892c8afbee09d16f480e6f9","heading":"Complaint – Requirements – Form.","ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":null,"schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.40.160:section","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.40.160","text":"A complaint shall be in writing and shall be signed by the complainant. More than one violation may be charged in the same complaint. A complaint shall be deemed sufficient if in substantially the same form of the complaint set forth in K.S.A. 12-4202 and amendments thereto or in substantially the following form:\nIN THE MUNICIPAL COURT OF TOPEKA, KANSAS\nThe City of Topeka, Kansas, vs. ________________________________\n________________________________\n(Accused person)\n________________________________\nThe undersigned, complains that on or about the _________________________ day of ______________, A.D., ________, in the City of Topeka, County of Shawnee, and State of Kansas, _______________\n________________________________\ndid then and there unlawfully __________\n________________________________\nin violation of Section ____ of Ordinance No. ________ of the City of Topeka, Kansas.\n_______________________ Complainant\n* Sworn to positively before me, this ____________________________ day of ____________________, A.D., ________\n______________________________ Officer authorized to administer oaths\n(*This complaint is not required to be sworn if it is signed by a law enforcement officer, the City Attorney, an Assistant City Attorney, an animal control officer, or a Fire Department employee with authority to enforce the Uniform Fire Code.)\n(Ord. 20206 § 9, 9-10-19; Ord. 17666 § 18, 3-27-01. Code 1995 § 50-53. Formerly 2.110.160.)\nCross References: Fire Department, TMC 2.20.030 ; City Attorney, TMC 2.20.070 ; Police Department, TMC 2.20.090 ; animal control officer, TMC 6.05.040 .\nState Law References: Similar State statute, K.S.A. 12-4202 .","type":"section","workbench_component_id":"184d4f8c-d8d9-526e-8033-153d6fa96c9b"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"2.40.160","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.40.160","content_hash":"8c17b70476f219435bd6325142e433ad37f8d1d0f38f7c3ca2e3bb8b029c48a4","heading":null,"ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.40.160:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.40.160:block:0","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.40.160","text":"A complaint shall be in writing and shall be signed by the complainant. More than one violation may be charged in the same complaint. A complaint shall be deemed sufficient if in substantially the same form of the complaint set forth in K.S.A. 12-4202 and amendments thereto or in substantially the following form:","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"0b2030c6-50a2-5f1f-8413-003941b61686"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"2.40.160","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.40.160","content_hash":"cba1edc1a1cfbc8f41c1298ced8da406d84edbe74cf9b79127f2fb2fcd1c8f77","heading":null,"ordinal":1,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.40.160:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.40.160:block:1","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.40.160","text":"IN THE MUNICIPAL COURT OF TOPEKA, KANSAS","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"dfcc84b6-80a0-57b7-98e6-abfe215e3fce"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"2.4